From 75227670d95c315c8f6c0c77fc0c281d461108c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 11:39:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] bfd: aarch64 PE: mark handled relocs with r_ignore

The ABS-constant ADRP rewrite marked the relocation as handled by setting
rel->r_vaddr = (bfd_vma) -1.  That marker was only honoured by the
cofflink.c hunk in our "Fix IMAGE_REL_ARM64_PAGEBASE_REL21 relocation and
symbol reduction" commit, which this rebase drops because upstream
supersedes it with a dedicated r_ignore field (2b0b52883eb), consumed at
bfd/cofflink.c:3116.

Left as-is the marker is written but never read, so the relocation is
processed normally and contents + rel->r_vaddr addresses memory at offset
(bfd_vma) -1.  Use upstream's mechanism instead.

Signed-off-by: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
---
 bfd/coff-aarch64.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bfd/coff-aarch64.c b/bfd/coff-aarch64.c
index df624109352..424e7aff0da 100644
--- a/bfd/coff-aarch64.c
+++ b/bfd/coff-aarch64.c
@@ -769,7 +769,7 @@ if (bfd_is_abs_section (sec)
                     contents + rel->r_vaddr);
 
         /* Mark this reloc handled so generic relocation won't touch it. */
-        rel->r_vaddr = (bfd_vma) -1;
+        rel->r_ignore = 1;
         break;
       }
   } 
